{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "pmat",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/paiml/aprender",
          "rules": []
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "commandLine": "pmat tdg / pmat analyze complexity --file on base and head copies (CLI); pmat query (index build); pmat MCP pmat_index_stats (answered); scripts/pr_review_duplication_scan.sh with PR_REVIEW_NEEDLE_MIN_LEN=20"
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "pmat.tdg-delta",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Per-file TDG, base vs head, on the 3 largest changed non-test .rs files (of 515 changed .rs; the rest were not scored): shapes.rs 78.0 (B) -> 77.8 (B); extract/code.rs 80.0 (B+) -> 80.0 (B+); commands/discharge.rs is new, 76.4 (B). No grade fell. Max cyclomatic in code.rs rose 7 -> 9 (max cognitive fell 23 -> 21); shapes.rs max cognitive 23 -> 20. stdout_sha256 below is the head run on shapes.rs; base/head copies were scored with the same command."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "pmat",
              "tdg",
              "crates/aprender-contracts/src/ontology/shapes.rs"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "de4441803781d49dabd6a361edbf28bd2545cdb91bfe5640e56e96b110609c83",
            "failure_scenario": "A TDG slide on the ontology shapes and extractor modules erodes the B floor across successive PRs; none fell a grade here, and 512 other changed .rs files were not scored.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "pmat.cb200-revert-no-dangling-refs",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The last commit removes scripts/check_cb200_tdg_grade.sh, scripts/cb200_baseline.rebaseline and the one-time re-baseline hooks. A tree-wide search (excluding evidence/, target/, .git/) for the two removed names finds them only in docs/audits/impl-PMAT-4588-receipts.md and docs/findings/cb200-main-green-over-baseline.jsonl: no workflow, script or contract still calls the deleted files."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "grep",
              "-rIl",
              "--exclude-dir=evidence",
              "--exclude-dir=target",
              "--exclude-dir=.git",
              "-e",
              "check_cb200_tdg_grade",
              "-e",
              "cb200_baseline.rebaseline",
              "."
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "113915410f0f6070f3a8df6cf53fd4f832d07f4a6afa7b3f23c498d7438c6080",
            "failure_scenario": "A caller of the deleted checker would fail closed or, worse, silently skip; none remains outside prose.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "pmat.cb200-stored-baseline-below-measured",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "After the revert the stored CB-200 baseline is main's 599 while the author's own same-scanner run measures 622 on base and 621 on head. The PR is never-worse (-1), but a gate that compares to the stored 599 would read RED on base and head alike; that is main's standing state (docs/findings/cb200-main-green-over-baseline.jsonl), not introduced here, and the raise was correctly dropped as a waiver."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "cited",
            "source": "docs/audits/impl-PMAT-4588-receipts.md",
            "excerpt": "head never-worse (-1); the 599->617 was a stored-limit raise, not new findings",
            "excerpt_sha256": "2e5b0b45521f7f90750410e8848ec4a787bdfe37ec85abc7351d58b1b0ebc0e2",
            "failure_scenario": "If CB-200 is later enforced against the stored 599 without first clearing main's over-baseline definitions, every PR is RED for a cause none of them introduced.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "pmat.duplication-scan",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Lexical duplication scan over HEAD, all 1148 unmerged sibling branches and merge_base..origin/main (0 files): 1661 needles (needle min length raised to 20 because the default 6 did not finish in over an hour on this 1925-file diff), 71 hits. 25 are HEAD name hits (test names in contracts/tests and doc prose), 46 are sibling-branch filename hits, concentrated on the stacked-split siblings m1/pv-publish-order, m1/shard-4..6, 89/m3-class-judge and 0d/3715-pr2-on-pr1 that carry the same files by construction. None read as an unrelated re-implementation. The scan is exact-name only: a renamed re-implementation is invisible to it."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "The scan output was read by the reviewer; the hit attribution (stacked siblings, not rivals) is judgement.",
            "failure_scenario": "A same-purpose re-implementation under a different name, or a sibling branch that already landed part of this fold, would not be found and would merge as new code.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "review.delta-fixture-b13",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Delta 331e4865be..1411fe2c51 (2 commits, +5/-5 lines). (1) ont4c5_capability_cells.rs: B goes 14 -> 13 by dropping qwen2-1.5b-q4km@gx10, matching contracts/model-capability-ladder-v1.yaml where that rung now reads hosts: [lambda] (#4590 G2 de-claim). The fixture can still fail: the probe requires every B id in the domain, so re-adding a de-claimed cell or losing a claimed one turns it RED; the row-deletion mutation was moved from qwen2 (no gx10 cell any more, so its assertion would be vacuous) to qwen35-0.8b-q4km, whose @gx10 cell is still in B, so the assertion names a real owed cell. (2) contracts.nt +1 line: model/host \"lambda\" for the qwen2 rung sha 6a1a2eb6, sorted between greenOn and id; extract/gguf.rs:256 emits one model/host triple per rung.hosts entry, and the two sibling de-claimed rungs (qwen3-1.7b, qwen3-8b) carry the identical shape. Read by diff and source only; pv extract was not run (cargo is forbidden on this host). No defect found in the delta. Residual: the qwen2 gx10 greenOn and parityReceipt triples remain as historical evidence, consistent with how the qwen3 rungs were left."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "cited",
            "source": "crates/aprender-contracts-cli/tests/ont4c5_capability_cells.rs",
            "excerpt": "\"qwen2-1.5b-q4km@lambda\", // G2 (#4590, operator 2026-09-28 16:15Z) de-claims qwen2 on gx10 through data",
            "excerpt_sha256": "09fb6c9ec6c8cee1dd6b188c9ccc27a88cef3559223c3854a92d5c09c2a347e0",
            "failure_scenario": "If the .nt line were hand-edited rather than generated, or B still listed qwen2-1.5b-q4km@gx10, the capability-cells probe would read RED (or the fixture would assert a cell nobody owes); neither holds at this head by static reading.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "nvidia-cuda-docs",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/paiml/aprender",
          "rules": []
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "commandLine": "mcp__nvidia-cuda-docs__search_cuda_docs x2 (the cuda-docs-reviewer agent could not be dispatched from this session; queries run inline)"
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "cuda.no-authority-found",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Query 'PTX st.global vector store alignment requirements for scatter of rows into a key-value cache' returned an unrelated cuTile SpMV sample and a cp.async.bulk.tensor excerpt; nothing on plain st.global alignment. The new gdn_kv_row_scatter_indirect kernel (dst[*pos_ptr*row+i]=src[i], one f32 per thread) is not shown to need vector alignment, and the docs neither support nor contradict that."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "The server returned unrelated samples; silence is not evidence.",
            "failure_scenario": "If the scatter is later vectorised to 16-byte stores, an unaligned cache row offset (row not a multiple of 4 floats) would fault; today's scalar stores are unaffected.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "cuda.shfl-sync-membermask",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The docs state shfl.sync is undefined if the executing thread is outside membermask (and results are undefined when sourcing from an inactive thread). The new decode_attention_split kernel scores with a warp-wide shfl.sync.down sum (its test asserts the mnemonic, decode_attention_split.rs:368). The builder helper it goes through (ptx/builder/sync.rs shfl_down_f32) hard-codes an immediate 31 in the clamp/mask position with the comment 'mask for 32 threads'; the reviewer did not verify on a device that every lane of the warp is active at each shuffle."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "cited",
            "source": "mcp__nvidia-cuda-docs__search_cuda_docs: warp shuffle reduction shfl.sync.bfly full mask semantics in split-K decode attention (PTX ISA shfl.sync)",
            "excerpt": "The behavior of `shfl.sync` is undefined if the executing thread is not in the `membermask`.",
            "excerpt_sha256": "d9f0fafa6f1dec1292e91b552d4cff17a832bdc0833e657eb93aec0f63dcf1f9",
            "failure_scenario": "If a tail warp of the split kernel has inactive lanes at a shfl.sync.down, the reduction reads undefined values and the attention score for that position is wrong without any fault.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "crux",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/paiml/aprender",
          "rules": []
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "commandLine": "guard predicates --match-comparative; contracts/apr-cli-commands-v1.yaml diff read; grep over contracts/crux-*.yaml"
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "crux.coverage-none",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "Surfaces: the new `apr ptx-debug` subcommand (analyze, gen-fkr, version) and the hidden `apr surface` command added to contracts/apr-cli-commands-v1.yaml, plus 8 further apr-cli registry lines for pv subcommands (challenge, discharge, obligations, ontology). A search of contracts/crux-*.yaml for `ptx-debug` finds no covering contract, so crux_coverage is none for that surface, which is itself a finding. No comparator claim (N x competitor) was added in book/, README or CHANGELOG lines of the diff that this review read by pattern."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "bash",
              "-c",
              "grep -l -e ptx-debug contracts/crux-*.yaml"
            ],
            "exit_code": 1,
            "stdout_sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855",
            "failure_scenario": "A user-facing CLI subcommand ships with no competitive contract, so a regression against the tool users would otherwise reach for cannot be seen by the crux ladder.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "cargo-mutants",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/paiml/aprender",
          "rules": []
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": false,
          "commandLine": "cargo mutants was not run",
          "toolExecutionNotifications": [
            {
              "level": "error",
              "message": {
                "text": "cargo mutants --in-diff was not attempted (attempted=0). The hard rules for this review forbid cargo test, nextest and cargo-mutants on this host (lambda). 515 .rs files are in the diff and the guard's --match-mutation-trigger fires on 667 of the 1925 changed paths, including scripts/check_*.sh guards (a 100% guard-mutation requirement, B3, that this review did not measure). The PR's own CI mutants job and the guard mutation set are the only measurements."
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "results": []
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "antigravity",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/paiml/aprender",
          "rules": []
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "commandLine": "agy -p <prompt file> --output-format json --json-schema .pr-review-schema.json --model gpt-oss-120b-medium --print-timeout 30m --dangerously-skip-permissions --add-dir <disposable tree> (attempts 1 and 2 returned 503 no capacity, attempt 3 succeeded)"
        }
      ],
      "results": []
    }
  ]
}